# Git push remotes

## Day-to-day (`dev` and topic work)

When pushing after merge to **`dev`** (or when the user asks to push the integration branch):

- Push **`dev`** to **both**:
  - **`betmundial`** (`Betmundial-ke/betmundial_web`)
  - **`origin`** (`tembulamusa/betmundia-web`)
- Prefer: `git push betmundial dev` and `git push origin dev` (set upstream on first push with `-u` on one or both remotes if needed).
- Do **not** push only one of these two unless the user explicitly scopes the push.

After a topic branch is merged into `dev` and `dev` is pushed:

- Delete the topic branch **locally** always.
- Delete it on the **remote** if it was pushed there (`git push <remote> --delete <branch>`).
- Do **not** delete `dev` or `master`.

## “All remotes”

When the user asks for **all remotes**, also push **`backup`** (`tembulamusa/betmundial-backup`).

## Safety

- Never force-push unless explicitly requested.
- Do not change git config.
- Do not mass-delete unrelated remote branches without checking.
- Branching model: see `git-workflow.mdc`.
